From: hmaarrfk <mark.harfouche@conda-forge.org>
Date: 2026-05-10
Subject: intel_npu: pin prebuilt vcl path to ubuntu22.04 (skip lsb_release)

`src/plugins/intel_npu/cmake/download_compiler_libs.cmake` gates the
download/install of the prebuilt vcl
(`libopenvino_intel_npu_compiler.so` / `libnpu_driver_compiler.so`)
on `lsb_release -is == "Ubuntu"` + a `22.04`/`24.04` version check.
The conda-forge build runs inside AlmaLinux 9 where `lsb_release` is
not installed, so OS_NAME/OS_VERSION come back empty and the whole
install block is silently skipped — the NPU plugin ends up without
the compiler library and users see `Failed to load
openvino_intel_npu_compiler` at runtime.

The recipe pre-fetches the ubuntu_22_04 prebuilt tarball at the same
on-disk path `download_and_extract()` looks for (so the function's
existence check short-circuits the file(DOWNLOAD) call and reuses
our copy).  This patch removes the lsb_release probe and just claims
Ubuntu 22.04 so the install + configure_file step is exercised.

The 22.04 prebuilt requires glibc 2.34 at runtime, which the
downstream conda package expresses via `__glibc >=2.34` on the
libopenvino-intel-npu-plugin output.
---
 src/plugins/intel_npu/cmake/download_compiler_libs.cmake | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/intel_npu/cmake/download_compiler_libs.cmake b/src/plugins/intel_npu/cmake/download_compiler_libs.cmake
index 3f34a73e..cd03bf5e 100644
--- a/src/plugins/intel_npu/cmake/download_compiler_libs.cmake
+++ b/src/plugins/intel_npu/cmake/download_compiler_libs.cmake
@@ -137,8 +137,15 @@ if(ENABLE_INTEL_NPU_COMPILER)
         # Check if the operating system is Linux and not macOS
         if(UNIX AND NOT APPLE)
             # Get the OS name and version
-            execute_process(COMMAND lsb_release -is OUTPUT_VARIABLE OS_NAME OUTPUT_STRIP_TRAILING_WHITESPACE)
-            execute_process(COMMAND lsb_release -rs OUTPUT_VARIABLE OS_VERSION OUTPUT_STRIP_TRAILING_WHITESPACE)
+            # conda-forge build runs on AlmaLinux 9 where lsb_release
+            # is not available; the upstream check would silently skip
+            # the prebuilt vcl install.  The vcl tarball is pre-fetched
+            # by the recipe at the same temp/compiler_libs/ubuntu22.04/
+            # path download_and_extract() expects, so just claim
+            # Ubuntu 22.04 here.  The downstream conda package adds a
+            # __glibc>=2.34 constraint to match the prebuilt's ABI.
+            set(OS_NAME "Ubuntu")
+            set(OS_VERSION "22.04")

             if(OS_NAME STREQUAL "Ubuntu")
                 if(OS_VERSION STREQUAL "22.04")
